      "id": "release",
      "name": "Release",
      "category": "IoBuffer",
      "signature": "Release(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FIoBuffer*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "nodiscard ] ] TIoStatusOr<uint8*>",
      "docs": "Relinquishes control of the internal buffer to the caller and removes it from the FIoBuffer.\nThis allows the caller to assume ownership of the internal data and prevent it from being deleted along with\nthe FIoBuffer.\nNOTE: It is only valid to call this if the FIoBuffer currently owns the internal memory allocation, as the\npoint of the call is to take ownership of it. If the FIoBuffer is only wrapping the allocation then it will\nreturn a failed FIoStatus instead.\n@return A status wrapper around the memory pointer. Even if the status is valid the pointer might still be null."
    },
